# Port patch, a bug of the prototype (tester report 06.11.2026: "the Killer7 is supposed to destroy wooden doors in
# a single shot, here they just break a single piece at a time"): the door's damage checks (emdoor.cpp) sorted the
# magnums (damage kinds 5 Broken Butterfly, 6 Killer7, 0xF Handcannon) and 0x2C with the rifles: one pane of a
# wooden door per shot (four panes break it), and on iron doors only the hit lock, from close by. The US, European
# and Japanese main.dol (emDoorDmCkWood, emDoorDmCkIron, emDoorDmCkIron2, emDoorDmCkIronDown, read with
# port/tools/retail_code.py) send them to the branch of the explosives: a wooden door breaks with its locks and
# chains in one shot, an iron door loses every lock and chain. The releases also ignore the thrown eggs (kinds
# 0x19, 0x1F, 0x20; the prototype's switch sent them to the explosive branch), break both locks of the falling
# door (type 2) like those of types 3 and 7, and (European and Japanese only) let no explosion break a locked
# wooden door (Be_flg bit 0). Now as the European release, with all discs.
